## attack.test.ts
@flow-hash: 3e133496

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant H as Human (Test Writer)
    participant T as attack.test.ts
    participant P as createGameDataProvider()
    participant A as applyAttack()
    participant D as resolveDamage()
    participant L as legalTargets()
    participant R as RNG stub
    participant U as Unit state mutation

    H->>T: Run test suite
    T->>P: Create game data provider
    P-->>T: provider
    T->>L: Check legal targets
    L->>P: Fetch unit templates
    P-->>L: Templates
    L-->>T: 'd' is target
    T->>D: Resolve damage
    D->>P: Fetch unit templates & moon phase
    P-->>D: Templates & moon
    D-->>T: Damage amount
    T->>A: Apply attack
    A->>P: Fetch unit templates
    P-->>A: Templates
    A->>U: Update defender HP
    A->>U: Mark attacker as acted
    U-->>A: Updated state
    A-->>T: New state
    T->>T: Assert HP reduced
    T->>T: Assert hasActed = true
    T->>T: Assert original state unchanged

    T->>T: Test out-of-range (no-op)
    T->>A: Apply attack (out of range)
    A-->>T: Return original state

    T->>T: Test ability with maladiction
    T->>A: Apply ability (frostbolt)
    A->>R: Use fixed RNG (roll = 0)
    R-->>A: Roll result
    A->>D: Resolve damage
    D-->>A: Damage amount
    A->>U: Apply damage
    A->>U: Apply maladiction (save lands)
    U-->>A: Updated state
    A-->>T: New state
    T->>T: Assert damage applied
    T->>T: Assert maladiction applied

    T->>T: Test ability with maladiction save fails
    T->>A: Apply ability (frostbolt)
    A->>R: Use fixed RNG (roll = 99)
    R-->>A: Roll result
    A->>D: Resolve damage
    D-->>A: Damage amount
    A->>U: Apply damage
    A->>U: Skip maladiction (save fails)
    U-->>A: Updated state
    A-->>T: New state
    T->>T: Assert damage applied
    T->>T: Assert maladiction NOT applied
```

Caption: The test suite orchestrates game state updates through attack and ability resolution, interacting with a data provider for templates and simulating deterministic RNG for maladiction outcomes.

## attack.ts
@flow-hash: 764d17bf

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant H as Human Player
    participant S as MatchState
    participant T as Token
    participant P as IGameDataProvider
    participant R as ISeededRng
    participant D as Damage Resolver
    participant L as Legal Target Checker
    participant A as Attack Function
    participant B as Ability Function
    participant M as Save Roller
    participant U as Unit Template Resolver

    H->>A: initiate attack
    A->>S: find attacker and target tokens
    A->>L: check if target is legal
    L-->>A: return legal target list
    A->>U: resolve attacker template
    A->>U: resolve defender template
    A->>D: calculate damage
    D-->>A: return damage amount
    A->>T: mark attacker as acted
    A->>T: apply damage to defender
    A-->>S: return updated state

    H->>B: cast ability
    B->>S: find caster and target tokens
    B->>U: resolve caster template
    B->>U: resolve target template
    B->>D: calculate damage (if any)
    D-->>B: return damage amount
    B->>M: roll save for maladiction
    M-->>B: return save result
    B->>T: mark caster as acted
    B->>T: apply damage to target (if any)
    B->>T: apply status effect (if save landed)
    B-->>S: return updated state
```

Caption: The human player initiates attacks or casts abilities, which are processed through token resolution, damage calculation, and status application across the game state.
